{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 89, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 89, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=90&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=88&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 459889026, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r459889026-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Eye opening, must visit", "text": "A trip to Nepal wouldn't be complete without visiting Pashupatinath Temple. It is the most important temple in Nepal, Hindus all around the world visit it all year round. That's why there's always so many people, but it's worth the visit. One can learn so much of Nepali culture through this place. Warning; it is not for the faint of heart!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "A0E3292404AECFE67C574C4812D79FAA", "name": "dorisp419", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/dorisp419", "username": "dorisp419", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ec/3d/default-avatar-2020-1.jpg", "contribution_count": 55, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 294265, "location_name": "Singapore", "location_name_detailed": "Singapore, Singapore"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-15", "published_at_date": "2017-02-15"}, {"review_id": 459870422, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r459870422-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Pilgrims", "text": "I always take my family to pilgrims to this place...though it's crowded but still like to go there and pray....", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C7FECE7875F65AB2E4CDE11FA814C10F", "name": "Sandhya Rani P", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/sandhyaranip", "username": "sandhyaranip", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e7/3d/default-avatar-2020-55.jpg", "contribution_count": 12, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-15", "published_at_date": "2017-02-15"}, {"review_id": 459737992, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r459737992-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Best religious place to visit  in worldwide", "text": "Best experience of my life,  felling so much blessed  after visiting their, only Indian and Nepal people's  are allowed  to enter in main mandir. No leather things allowed inside. \nHigh security  of police and military their. Many shops were located near about the temple  either  of food or religious things to buy.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2016-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "DBA02469AD41D5E25566FA8C267C138E", "name": "Prateek J", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/312prateekj", "username": "312prateekj", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0b/1b/08/1f/prateek-j.jpg", "contribution_count": 18, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-14", "published_at_date": "2017-02-15"}, {"review_id": 459066683, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r459066683-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Also includes the crematoria", "text": "If you are interested to watch how the local people burn the bodies of their relatives that passed away. Please don't take your children, It also includes a hindu temple and you have to pay 1500 rupee or 15 $ as entrance fee. the place is not clean but it is a very important part of the local life.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4BE9CA8ECD8E71C58B603BFE87B07C9A", "name": "ibrahimarab", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ibrahimarab", "username": "ibrahimarab", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/2c/6a/4a/a5/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 39, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-13", "published_at_date": "2017-02-13"}, {"review_id": 458711046, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r458711046-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Big majestic temple ", "text": "Among the largest temples in Nepal, this temple frames an important religious value to the Hindus. The Nandi idol is huge!! \n\nThe infrastructure is again very poor by the authorities. Watchout for the monkeys!!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "91D2AE2608F537BD2CF554B341FB2EE2", "name": "rohitkulthia", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/rohitkulthia", "username": "rohitkulthia", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/12/66/2e/d9/rohitkulthia.jpg", "contribution_count": 127, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304551, "location_name": "New Delhi", "location_name_detailed": "New Delhi, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-11", "published_at_date": "2017-02-12"}, {"review_id": 458441562, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r458441562-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Vacation ", "text": "This is another great way to spend the day.  Great bathing pool and historical buildings. Fun to explore the city with the restaurants and shops. \nA half day or less is all that is needed.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "B195BD813E012F326AF7E17FBE4706FD", "name": "Perry H", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/PERRYMERLIN", "username": "PERRYMERLIN", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/03/3e/dc/df/perry-h.jpg", "contribution_count": 1757, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 60750, "location_name": "San Diego", "location_name_detailed": "San Diego, California"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-10", "published_at_date": "2017-02-10"}, {"review_id": 458299673, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r458299673-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Interesting and fascinating but getting expensive", "text": "The Pashupatinath temple is extremly fascinating for a good look into Hindu culture in Kathmandu, and if you have the time, it's worth the visit. But the last few years the price for entering have just gone up, and it is getting rather expensive (1000 rupees)", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "340A636D86DA074191BD088626C1F15B", "name": "Peter Andersen", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/peteraB6859EU", "username": "peteraB6859EU", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/4f/47/83/peter-a.jpg", "contribution_count": 638, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 806258, "location_name": "Aars", "location_name_detailed": "Aars, Denmark"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-09", "published_at_date": "2017-02-10"}, {"review_id": 458243886, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r458243886-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Om Nama Sivaya - Best Place To visit", "text": "This is the temple of Lord Shiva, thousands of travelers visit every day here. If you are Hindu you can go inside the temple main area also. You wan watch various traditions and culture of Hindus around here.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2016-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "E36D516E344927D07AE69583B7EEDF71", "name": "Pushpendra Khadka", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/KhadkaPushpendra", "username": "KhadkaPushpendra", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/e7/e6/a9/pushpendra-k.jpg", "contribution_count": 52, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-09", "published_at_date": "2017-02-09"}, {"review_id": 457828085, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r457828085-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "DENiED ADMiSSiON", "text": "(1) What a wild concept: CHARGE Foreigners an admission fee (1000 Rupees), but DENY them access to the temple.\n(2) Still the grounds are interesting and you may see a BURiAL.  1st they bathe the body by the river then they take it away for cremation.\n(3) Aggressive MACAQUES monkeying around.  Keep yr things secured.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "035353FF88A00CCA4FFFE705C779BF97", "name": "Pali Aha", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/SoundOfPurple", "username": "SoundOfPurple", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1b/75/37/cd/pali-a.jpg", "contribution_count": 665, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 6999277, "location_name": "Waikiki", "location_name_detailed": "Waikiki, Hawaii"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-07", "published_at_date": "2017-02-08"}, {"review_id": 457817681, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r457817681-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Scores of Shiva Temples in Ruins", "text": "If you go to Kathmandu and do not visit Pashupatinath Temple, your visit would be incomplete.\nA historical monument, much revered by Hindus from across the Globe, is on the banks of a small river. The main temple is in tact but scores of small small temple on the other side of the stream are practically in ruins. However these are a \"must see\". Many miss this aspect as just behind the temple is a cremation site where one would invariably find a cremation taking place (One avoids going on the other side).\nOverall a good tourist spot plus a religous monument.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "E66F338BA5A6E4585EC1812B8F871580", "name": "Ved Prakash M", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/513vedprakashm", "username": "513vedprakashm", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ec/a2/default-avatar-2020-3.jpg", "contribution_count": 10, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1162496, "location_name": "Meerut", "location_name_detailed": "Meerut, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-07", "published_at_date": "2017-02-08"}, {"review_id": 457004828, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r457004828-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Beautiful temple with terrible people", "text": "Do not get a guide at all cost. AT. ALL. COST. \nGuides are out for money and will pretend to be your friend and ask for any amount you want. \nGuide will bring you to \"holy men\" who will have a picture to be taken and request for 20USD. Guide boasted to us that \"holy men\" will even charge up to 60USD for white tourists. \nGuide then brought us to another set of \"holy men\" who will \"bless you\" for another 20USD. Honestly do not know what their religion it is to. \nIt is honestly a beautiful temple filled with tradition and heritage so do not let a guide ruin this experience like it did for us.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 1, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2016-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C9D1A50047A76FC92C17FF13B7C7AF05", "name": "Jxketan", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/jxketan", "username": "jxketan", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/18/40/28/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 30, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/56/55/c6/photo0jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-02-04", "published_at_date": "2017-02-07"}, {"review_id": 457076723, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r457076723-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "very holy place", "text": "One of the highlights for HIndus and the real hindus can even enter the centre of this place, which westerners can not join. To pay 1000Nrs per visit is ok, but no too nice. You can walk around and see old temples and you can watch to the cremation of the dead bodies here", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1BF60FE7B209304B099CF14472FF4567", "name": "lalbaba108", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/lalbaba108", "username": "lalbaba108", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e3/1f/default-avatar-2020-46.jpg", "contribution_count": 101, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 424934, "location_name": "Bhaktapur", "location_name_detailed": "Bhaktapur, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/57/02/eb/old-temples.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/57/02/f3/panorama-view.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/57/02/f8/cremation.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/57/02/fa/the-holy-center.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/57/02/fe/pagoda.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-02-04", "published_at_date": "2017-02-05"}, {"review_id": 457074157, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r457074157-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "very cosmic place", "text": "One the most holy places for Hindus and only real Hindus can enter the centre of this place. HUge area full of old temples and the cremation of the dead bodies you can watch here very good. Wonderful place !!!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "CC940FAFEC9C51E42F57AE083F6FB5C3", "name": "christoph s", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/christophs2512", "username": "christophs2512", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/23/86/2d/6e/lal-c.jpg", "contribution_count": 30, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1993162, "location_name": "Bokel", "location_name_detailed": "Bokel, Germany"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-04", "published_at_date": "2017-02-04"}, {"review_id": 456913053, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r456913053-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A most impressive sight", "text": "For me, the Pashupatinath Temple was a most impressive sight was. This is also known as the crematorium. It may sound morbid or gross, but in the presence of people caring for, and venerating their dead, I felt an empathy for the mourners, and a glimpse of something sacred in their lives.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1DCAC13D3AFFEFC437F87419AEDE2ED1", "name": "eileen5321", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/eileen5321", "username": "eileen5321", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/05/e6/90/24/eileen5321.jpg", "contribution_count": 136, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/55/6b/ec/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/55/6b/ff/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/55/6c/15/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/55/6c/1b/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/55/6c/32/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/55/6c/44/pashupatinath-temple.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-02-03", "published_at_date": "2017-02-04"}, {"review_id": 456877311, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r456877311-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A religious site, not a tourist site", "text": "I hated the tourist experience. As much as I respect the religious aspect, 1000NPR for that experience (or should I say inexperience?) was steeper than the Himalayas. I saw little. Non-Hindus are not permitted in most parts. In fact even western-Hindus are not permitted in many parts. Without clear signage, expect to walk beyond the boundaries and get shouted at. It is embarrassing and shameful. If you open your doors to guests, be clear. I was massively curious and ultimately disappointed. I'm not religious and this was the equivalent of opening a Christmas present, only to lose the ability of eyes, hands and ears to know what the gift was. Also, for the whole of the paid experience, I was tailed by several beggars. I did not enjoy it.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 2, "subratings": [], "like_count": 3, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "E1E30780988B547E3F149DEACEA05035", "name": "acton28.blog", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/oyster28catcher", "username": "oyster28catcher", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/08/46/60/f9/acton28.jpg", "contribution_count": 384, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 187069, "location_name": "Manchester", "location_name_detailed": "Manchester, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-03", "published_at_date": "2017-02-03"}, {"review_id": 456526305, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r456526305-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Temple with golden roof", "text": "This is a temple about 6 kms away from the city. This temple has several layers and uniqueness is its golden roof and silver doors.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2016-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "D8113713EA3BA3890237152CF4BD58DF", "name": "Dilip P", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/686dilipp", "username": "686dilipp", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e3/1f/default-avatar-2020-46.jpg", "contribution_count": 615, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 297613, "location_name": "Vadodara", "location_name_detailed": "Vadodara, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-02-01", "published_at_date": "2017-02-02"}, {"review_id": 456074935, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r456074935-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Cremation complex - sombre but moving", "text": "Whereas temple itself is open only to Hindus, the cremation ghats nearby are easily viewed from across the disgustingly polluted Bagmati river ( a stream in January). Cremation ceremonies can be viewed discreetly.\n", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2017-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "081FA483594C3DBB540A4B8B054074A2", "name": "Marek R", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/142marekr", "username": "142marekr", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/df/99/default-avatar-2020-40.jpg", "contribution_count": 57, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 181778, "location_name": "Port Alberni", "location_name_detailed": "Port Alberni, Canada"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-01-31", "published_at_date": "2017-01-31"}, {"review_id": 456068880, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r456068880-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Kathmandu day tour", "text": "Visited the Pashupatinath Temple as part of a Kathmandu day tour with Himilayan Spirit.\n\nThis is a beautiful and very holy sight (From my understanding- the most holy Hindu sight in all of Nepal). Our guide was great at explainingall the cultural traditions to us, otherwise I think it would have all been a bit confusing. During our visit there was a Hindu funeral taking place on the river bank- very fascinating to see. \nI would recommend that you combine this attraction with the other main attractions of Kathmandu in a day tour (Monkey temple, Patan durbar square and Pashupatinath.). Enough to keep you busy for the full day and experience Nepalese culture at it's best. \nWe chose Himilayan Spirit adventures and could not recommend them highly enough- by far the best value for money (~65USD per person, Lonely Planet advertises one for the exact same things which is $95USD)) and included all entrance fees (which themselves equate to about ~30USD), a VERY informative and friendly tour guide and a driver with a nice, modern car. Could not recommend them more highly.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "8ADD3418AD33B717CE9EB554770E7676", "name": "Adelle J", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Adelle1947504638", "username": "Adelle1947504638", "avatar": null, "contribution_count": 43, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 658994, "location_name": "Main Beach", "location_name_detailed": "Main Beach, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-01-31", "published_at_date": "2017-01-31"}, {"review_id": 456055161, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r456055161-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Lame", "text": "Did not enjoy my visit to this temple. \n\nVery expensive entry fee of 1000nes. For this they don't actually let you go inside just the grounds \n\n There are lots of bits that tourists aren't allowed into but none of them are signed so when you walk in you get shouted at aggressively by nasty security people. \n\nThere are lots of beggars and people harrasing you inside so you can't even really sit and enjoy the atmosphere.  ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 1, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "AC1261B6FF627E5E57F008AD7DC56BCD", "name": "McAlice P", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/mcalicep", "username": "mcalicep", "avatar": null, "contribution_count": 30, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/4c/81/cc/20170130-104242-largejpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/4c/81/cd/20170130-104241-largejpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-01-31", "published_at_date": "2017-01-31"}, {"review_id": 455921088, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r455921088-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "High cultural value site", "text": "For those who wish to understand Nepalese culture, this is a must. The open-air cremations are unusual for Westerners to experience, but it's an integral part of Nepali Hindu culture.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2016-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C6943FA61393417E51E0642ADFC45CC5", "name": "Gaetan R", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/GaetanR92", "username": "GaetanR92", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f1/42/default-avatar-2020-20.jpg